      "filename": "02_Martin_Luther.md",
      "start": 623,
      "content": "Luther's other major works on the Jews were his 60,000-word treatise Von den Juden und Ihren Lügen (On the Jews and Their Lies), and Vom Schem Hamphoras und vom Geschlecht Christi (On the Holy Name and the Lineage of Christ), both published in 1543, three years before his death.",
      "semanticScore": 0.48317042790755893,
      "lexicalScore": null
    }
  ],
  "sentence_evidence": [
    {
      "documentId": "33cb2e92-97e1-4d7a-9b7d-db4371e45300",
      "value": "It has won the Short Form of the Hugo Award for Best Dramatic Presentation, the oldest science fiction/fantasy award for films and series, six times (every year since 2006, except for 2009, 2013 and 2014).",
      "start": 27,
      "end": 232,
      "similarity": 0.19709264661354683,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "33cb2e92-97e1-4d7a-9b7d-db4371e45300",
      "value": "The winning episodes were \"The Empty Child\"/\"The Doctor Dances\" (2006), \"The Girl in the Fireplace\" (2007), \"Blink\" (2008), \"The Waters of Mars\" (2010), \"The Pandorica Opens\"/\"The Big Bang\" (2011), and \"The Doctor's Wife\" (2012).",
      "start": 233,
      "end": 462,
      "similarity": -0.009566881856564033,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "33cb2e92-97e1-4d7a-9b7d-db4371e45300",
      "value": "Doctor Who star Matt Smith won Best Actor in the 2012 National Television awards alongside Karen Gillan who won Best Actress.",
      "start": 463,
      "end": 588,
      "similarity": -0.10091652272190417,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "33cb2e92-97e1-4d7a-9b7d-db4371e45300",
      "value": "Doctor Who has been nominated for over 200 awards and has won over a hundred of them.",
      "start": 589,
      "end": 674,
      "similarity": 0.1140843037889648,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "33cb2e92-97e1-4d7a-9b7d-db4371e45300",
      "value": "In addition to those actors who have headlined the series, others have portrayed versions of the Doctor in guest roles.",
      "start": 689,
      "end": 808,
      "similarity": -0.0606556599836412,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "33cb2e92-97e1-4d7a-9b7d-db4371e45300",
      "value": "Notably, in 2013, John Hurt guest-starred as a hitherto unknown incarnation of the Doctor known as the War Doctor in the run-up to the show's 50th anniversary special \"The Day of the Doctor\".",
      "start": 809,
      "end": 1000,
      "similarity": 0.003152248887919001,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "33cb2e92-97e1-4d7a-9b7d-db4371e45300",
      "value": "He is shown in mini-episode \"The Night of the Doctor\" to have been retroactively inserted into the show's fictional chronology between McGann and Eccleston's Doctors, although his introduction was written so as not to disturb the established numerical naming of the Doctors.",
      "start": 1001,
      "end": 1275,
      "similarity": 0.10089229341503846,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "33cb2e92-97e1-4d7a-9b7d-db4371e45300",
      "value": "Another example is from the 1986 serial The Trial of a Time Lord, where Michael Jayston portrayed the Valeyard, who is described as an amalgamation of the darker sides of the Doctor's nature, somewhere between his twelfth and final incarnation.",
      "start": 1276,
      "end": 1520,
      "similarity": 0.0701176785997957,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "16e26e01-cea7-414f-b18e-ef1511eda940",
      "value": "Luther sympathised with some of the peasants' grievances, as he showed in his response to the Twelve Articles in May 1525, but he reminded the aggrieved to obey the temporal authorities.",
      "start": 30,
      "end": 216,
      "similarity": 0.2052984452238562,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "16e26e01-cea7-414f-b18e-ef1511eda940",
      "value": "During a tour of Thuringia, he became enraged at the widespread burning of convents, monasteries, bishops' palaces, and libraries.",
      "start": 217,
      "end": 347,
      "similarity": 0.10797345838498724,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "16e26e01-cea7-414f-b18e-ef1511eda940",
      "value": "In Against the Murderous, Thieving Hordes of Peasants, written on his return to Wittenberg, he gave his interpretation of the Gospel teaching on wealth, condemned the violence as the devil's work, and called for the nobles to put down the rebels like mad dogs:",
      "start": 348,
      "end": 608,
      "similarity": 0.24718169449959954,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "16e26e01-cea7-414f-b18e-ef1511eda940",
      "value": "Luther's other major works on the Jews were his 60,000-word treatise Von den Juden und Ihren Lügen (On the Jews and Their Lies), and Vom Schem Hamphoras und vom Geschlecht Christi (On the Holy Name and the Lineage of Christ), both published in 1543, three years before his death.",
      "start": 623,
      "end": 902,
      "similarity": 0.48317042790755893,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "16e26e01-cea7-414f-b18e-ef1511eda940",
      "value": "Luther argued that the Jews were no longer the chosen people but \"the devil's people\", and referred to them with violent, vile language.",
      "start": 903,
      "end": 1039,
      "similarity": 0.15232313777390508,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "16e26e01-cea7-414f-b18e-ef1511eda940",
      "value": "Citing Deuteronomy 13, wherein Moses commands the killing of idolaters and the burning of their cities and property as an offering to God, Luther called for a \"scharfe Barmherzigkeit\" (\"sharp mercy\") against the Jews \"to see whether we might save at least a few from the glowing flames.\"",
      "start": 1040,
      "end": 1327,
      "similarity": 0.10276228913212525,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "16e26e01-cea7-414f-b18e-ef1511eda940",
      "value": "Luther advocated setting synagogues on fire, destroying Jewish prayerbooks, forbidding rabbis from preaching, seizing Jews' property and money, and smashing up their homes, so that these \"envenomed worms\" would be forced into labour or expelled \"for all time\".",
      "start": 1328,
      "end": 1588,
      "similarity": 0.1771552403079544,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "16e26e01-cea7-414f-b18e-ef1511eda940",
      "value": "In Robert Michael's view, Luther's words \"We are at fault in not slaying them\" amounted to a sanction for murder.",
      "start": 1589,
      "end": 1702,
      "similarity": 0.11292674201621365,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "16e26e01-cea7-414f-b18e-ef1511eda940",
      "value": "\"God's anger with them is so intense,\" Luther concluded, \"that gentle mercy will only tend to make them worse, while sharp mercy will reform them but little.",
      "start": 1703,
      "end": 1860,
      "similarity": 0.07404548058463453,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "16e26e01-cea7-414f-b18e-ef1511eda940",
      "value": "Therefore, in any case, away with them!\"",
      "start": 1861,
      "end": 1901,
      "similarity": -0.007976624221641066,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "adcbb821-906b-4b5b-b559-4e28fb475c3f",
      "value": "However, some computational problems are easier to analyze in terms of more unusual resources.",
      "start": 48,
      "end": 142,
      "similarity": 0.15657161757781174,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "adcbb821-906b-4b5b-b559-4e28fb475c3f",
      "value": "For example, a non-deterministic Turing machine is a computational model that is allowed to branch out to check many different possibilities at once.",
      "start": 143,
      "end": 292,
      "similarity": 0.008789155180540053,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "adcbb821-906b-4b5b-b559-4e28fb475c3f",
      "value": "The non-deterministic Turing machine has very little to do with how we physically want to compute algorithms, but its branching exactly captures many of the mathematical models we want to analyze, so that non-deterministic time is a very important resource in analyzing computational problems.",
      "start": 293,
      "end": 586,
      "similarity": 0.014288918296488796,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "adcbb821-906b-4b5b-b559-4e28fb475c3f",
      "value": "A problem is regarded as inherently difficult if its solution requires significant resources, whatever the algorithm used.",
      "start": 601,
      "end": 723,
      "similarity": 0.1154013768098448,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "adcbb821-906b-4b5b-b559-4e28fb475c3f",
      "value": "The theory formalizes this intuition, by introducing mathematical models of computation to study these problems and quantifying the amount of resources needed to solve them, such as time and storage.",
      "start": 724,
      "end": 923,
      "similarity": 0.11067037798008815,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "adcbb821-906b-4b5b-b559-4e28fb475c3f",
      "value": "Other complexity measures are also used, such as the amount of communication (used in communication complexity), the number of gates in a circuit (used in circuit complexity) and the number of processors (used in parallel computing).",
      "start": 924,
      "end": 1157,
      "similarity": 0.04441663235640683,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "adcbb821-906b-4b5b-b559-4e28fb475c3f",
      "value": "One of the roles of computational complexity theory is to determine the practical limits on what computers can and cannot do.",
      "start": 1158,
      "end": 1283,
      "similarity": 0.12135763091883442,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "7ccda51e-bfbb-4116-b410-e11a1c649bd3",
      "value": "Some argue that The United Methodist Church can lay a claim on apostolic succession, as understood in the traditional sense.",
      "start": 40,
      "end": 164,
      "similarity": -0.03234864338442822,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "7ccda51e-bfbb-4116-b410-e11a1c649bd3",
      "value": "As a result of the American Revolution, John Wesley was compelled in 1784 to break with standard practice and ordain two of his lay preachers as presbyters, Thomas Vasey and Richard Whatcoat.",
      "start": 165,
      "end": 356,
      "similarity": 0.17023009724048432,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "7ccda51e-bfbb-4116-b410-e11a1c649bd3",
      "value": "Dr. Thomas Coke, already an Anglican priest, assisted Wesley in this action.",
      "start": 357,
      "end": 433,
      "similarity": 0.021835424064982647,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "7ccda51e-bfbb-4116-b410-e11a1c649bd3",
      "value": "Coke was then \"set apart\" as a superintendent (bishop) by Wesley and dispatched with Vasey and Whatcoat to America to take charge of Methodist activities there.",
      "start": 434,
      "end": 594,
      "similarity": 0.06389021978493055,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "7ccda51e-bfbb-4116-b410-e11a1c649bd3",
      "value": "In defense of his action to ordain, Wesley himself cited an ancient opinion from the Church of Alexandria, which held that bishops and presbyters constituted one order and therefore, bishops are to be elected from and by the presbyterate.",
      "start": 595,
      "end": 833,
      "similarity": 0.08397496038530602,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "7ccda51e-bfbb-4116-b410-e11a1c649bd3",
      "value": "He knew that for two centuries the succession of bishops in the Church of Alexandria was preserved through ordination by presbyters alone and was considered valid by the ancient church.",
      "start": 834,
      "end": 1019,
      "similarity": 0.08229854974169912,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "7ccda51e-bfbb-4116-b410-e11a1c649bd3",
      "value": "Methodists today who would argue for apostolic succession would do so on these grounds.",
      "start": 1020,
      "end": 1107,
      "similarity": -0.043366716154597744,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "7ccda51e-bfbb-4116-b410-e11a1c649bd3",
      "value": "Nevertheless, The United Methodist Church \"implore[s] families and churches not to reject or condemn lesbian and gay members and friends\" and commits itself to be in ministry with all persons, affirming that God's grace, love, and forgiveness is available to all.",
      "start": 1122,
      "end": 1385,
      "similarity": -0.047832656753660996,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "7ccda51e-bfbb-4116-b410-e11a1c649bd3",
      "value": "Additionally, many organizations, conferences, and congregations have recently called for broader acceptance of the LGBT community within the UMC.",
      "start": 1386,
      "end": 1532,
      "similarity": 0.022835067771826575,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "7ccda51e-bfbb-4116-b410-e11a1c649bd3",
      "value": "For example, the Connectional Table, a governing committee, has voted in favor of a proposal that calls for a localized option, which would permit ministers to officiate same-sex weddings, and it would allow conferences to ordain gay clergy.",
      "start": 1533,
      "end": 1774,
      "similarity": 0.08964704217382401,
      "facetSimilarities": []
    },
    {
      "documentId": "7ccda51e-bfbb-4116-b410-e11a1c649bd3",
      "value": "Moreover, many conferences have taken a position by voting in favor of same-gender marriages with resolutions.",
      "start": 1775,
      "end": 1885,
      "similarity": 0.10236757461468603,
